+milestone: 2026.06.385
+milestone_title: "Reach the faithful baseline via the LIVE CONTIGUOUS run (NOT the broken bounded-pass chain) -> DECIDE the verifier moat with an ARBITER-grounded rerank-recovery test that is decision-grade at the INTERMEDIATE baseline, plus the full verifier-as-reward graft if val crosses 0.85"
+milestone_doc: openspec/change-proposals/research-roadmap-v385.md
+milestone_doc_summary: |
+  Planner (Opus 4.8) 2026-06-13. ROOT-CAUSE CORRECTION of .384: the "max_epochs epoch-fix" was a
+  MISDIAGNOSIS. exp4146 did NOT fail to train -- it never STARTED. A pre-launch guard
+  (diagnose_epoch_cap -> _noop_reason_for_diagnosis) read a STALE Lightning Timer state
+  (time_elapsed.train=3641.99s) baked into the checkpoint from a prior bounded pass, saw
+  timer_elapsed >= max_time, and emitted blocked_noop_cap_not_confirmed_timer_elapsed WITHOUT
+  launching the trainer (duration_s=0.121, post_epoch==seed_epoch==6399, val=null). config_max_epochs
+  was 50000 and epoch 6399, so the cap was NEVER the cause. The BOUNDED-PASS chain (resume -> 60-min
+  pass -> write back -> next pass) is the broken mechanism: it re-triggers the stale-Timer guard, the
+  global_step==0 progress-callback dead code, and the every-100-epoch write-back race.
+
+  THE REAL FIX IS ALREADY DEPLOYED AND WORKING. An operator-launched SINGLE 12-hour CONTIGUOUS run
+  (PID 432538) resumes once from the intact 0.278 checkpoint, restores the manual LR step, runs
+  continuously, validates every 100 epochs, and persists progress via save_last. Measured live this
+  session: val 0.199 floor -> 0.278 (.384 seed) -> 0.372 -> 0.426 and climbing ~+1.3-1.9pp / 100
+  epochs. The contiguous mechanism WORKS where the bounded-pass chain failed.
+
+  THE STRATEGIC RISK .385 MUST RETIRE: the decisive verifier-as-REWARD graft (the result that
+  resolves the moat + the queued DiffusionGemma gate) is gated on val>=0.85, which likely will NOT
+  land inside .385's execution window. .382/.383/.384 ALL produced no decisive moat verdict because
+  each was 100% blocked on reaching the faithful baseline. .385 BREAKS that pattern: it adds an
+  ARBITER-grounded (arXiv:2605.26172) verifier-RERANK RECOVERY test that is decision-grade at ANY
+  intermediate baseline WITH MEASURED HEADROOM (oracle@K > vote@1). ARBITER's core finding -- the
+  correct answer is frequently PRESENT-BUT-OUT-VOTED, and internal-signal verifiers "measure
+  self-consistency rather than correctness" and DEGRADE the vote -- is the exact existential question
+  Carnot calls the verifier moat. The EXECUTABLE Sudoku verifier is high-precision and ORTHOGONAL to
+  the generator's vote (it checks constraint validity, not generator confidence), which is precisely
+  the property ARBITER says an external verifier needs to BEAT self-consistency. So Sudoku-rerank is
+  the cleanest possible moat testbed, and it is MORE informative at a LOWER (high-headroom) baseline,
+  not less. The full A=verifier-cert vs B=vote-cert RFT graft stays DEFENSIVE on val>=0.85 (the
+  publishable de-confound); the rerank-recovery test carries the moat signal for .385 regardless.
+
+  NORTH STAR (ARC-AGI-3): .384 offline game-solving plateaued (no unsolved strict non-spatial
+  candidates; total stuck at 13). .385 pivots the ARC slot from "solve another game" to the
+  EFFICIENCY axis (north-star first-class metric): an OFFLINE, air-gapped verifier-as-action-pruner
+  measured against a random/greedy baseline (actions-to-solve), the prerequisite for the
+  offline-beats-baseline gate that precedes any online play (quota-conserve discipline preserved).
+
+  DiffusionGemma energy-guidance probe (flagged_for_v385) stays GATED: it activates ONLY after the
+  Sudoku graft reports verifier_value_added==true, which cannot happen until the baseline is faithful.
+  So .385 keeps it queued -- the rerank + graft work feeds its gate; the capstone records whether the
+  rerank discrimination signal moves it.
 
